{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1519966-would-serial-killers-choice-of-prey-escalate-when-they-transition-into-a-splat","id":1519966,"title":"Would serial killers' choice of prey escalate when they transition into a splat?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-08-06T10:00:55-07:00","id":1519966,"title":"Would serial killers' choice of prey escalate when they transition into a splat?","content":"I read an <a href=\"https://leb.fbi.gov/articles/featured-articles/the-link-between-animal-cruelty-and-human-violencet\" target=\"_blank\">article</a> that was posted on the LEB (Law Enforcement Bulletin), that talks about how animal abuse could lead to future acts of violence against people, such as assault, murder, etc. So that got me thinking, if a mortal serial killer was to be embraced into a vampire, or awakened as a mage, or learn that they are a werewolf, etc. Would that change their preference of victims from regular humans to supernatural beings similar to them?<br /> <br /> I ask this because all the splats in one way or another seem to look down on regular humans, with a few treating them either slightly better or worse than actual animals. Would their tendency to prey on regular humans as a normal mortal be a predictor of them preying on their fellow supernaturals?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/pub/18.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","name":"Hello","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-06T11:41:00-07:00","id":1519975,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hello</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1519966-would-serial-killers-choice-of-prey-escalate-when-they-transition-into-a-splat#post1519966\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I read an <a href=\"https://leb.fbi.gov/articles/featured-articles/the-link-between-animal-cruelty-and-human-violencet\" target=\"_blank\">article</a> that was posted on the LEB (Law Enforcement Bulletin), that talks about how animal abuse could lead to future acts of violence against people, such as assault, murder, etc. So that got me thinking, if a mortal serial killer was to be embraced into a vampire, or awakened as a mage, or learn that they are a werewolf, etc. Would that change their preference of victims from regular humans to supernatural beings similar to them?<br /> <br /> I ask this because all the splats in one way or another seem to look down on regular humans, with a few treating them either slightly better or worse than actual animals. Would their tendency to prey on regular humans as a normal mortal be a predictor of them preying on their fellow supernaturals?</div> </div> </div> </div>Unlikely that the <b>just </b>the transformation will change the preferences for a Supernatural being. First it will imply that the scale of satisfaction goes: Animals -&gt; Humans -&gt; Supernatural creatures, and nothing in the transformations refers tothis (except if the victim has to be challenging, like hunting the most dangerous possible prey).<br /> <br /> If they are into the abuse, a regular human is even more defenseless now that they face a serial killer that has mystical means.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","user":"lbeaumanior","date":". 08-06-2023, 04:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-06T12:53:26-07:00","id":1519978,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hello</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1519966-would-serial-killers-choice-of-prey-escalate-when-they-transition-into-a-splat#post1519966\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I ask this because all the splats in one way or another seem to look down on regular humans, with a few treating them either slightly better or worse than actual animals. Would their tendency to prey on regular humans as a normal mortal be a predictor of them preying on their fellow supernaturals?</div> </div> </div> </div>Would it be a predictor of them being capable of abusing and harming other supernaturals? Yes, because it's an indicator that they enjoy abuse and harm. Would it be a predictor of them <i>no longer </i>abusing and harming ordinary humans? No. They're not in it for the challenge, it's not an expression of peerdom. They'll probably continue to harm whoever they are around who is convenient to harm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-14T20:55:55-07:00","id":1520644,"title":"","content":"I believe his preferences would remain, often serial killers choose targets of opportunity and that are easy, assuming they don't have a predilection for a given type of victim, what can differentiate are their methods, in the case of the vampire and the werewolves it can even feed on his victims. As for other supernaturals, I believe he would avoid them as much as possible, after all he doesn't want to pick a fight, just do what he wants, but if he is the type that likes a challenge, I believe he will hunt them down eventually. If it's good to the point to cause trouble for the factions, I think this would be an interesting enemy in a cross-over.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}